From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:57:22 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: h264, vp8: clear the codec state on start

The codec state of a context is a union, and a context can change codecs
while its queues are stopped. The H.264 and VP8 start callbacks set the
sizes of their deblocking and intra prediction buffers only for pictures
wider than 2048 pixels, and their stop callbacks free these buffers when
the sizes are not zero. A narrower stream started after another codec in
the same context, or (H.264) after a wider stream, could find stale
non-zero sizes: the decoder then used stale buffer addresses, and
stopping freed buffers this stream never allocated.

Clear the codec's part of the union on start, as the MPEG-2 start
callback already does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c | 6 ++++++
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp8.c  | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
index 925514c9f..2dd7feda6 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
@@ -576,6 +576,12 @@ static int cedrus_h264_start(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
 	unsigned int pic_info_size;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The codec state is a union: clear what another codec, or a wider
+	 * stream, left in it.
+	 */
+	memset(&ctx->codec.h264, 0, sizeof(ctx->codec.h264));
+
 	/*
 	 * NOTE: All buffers allocated here are only used by HW, so we
 	 * can add DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING flag when allocating them.
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp8.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp8.c
index 954c0ceb9..a2d40ddb0 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp8.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp8.c
@@ -849,6 +849,12 @@ static int cedrus_vp8_start(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
 
+	/*
+	 * The codec state is a union: clear what another codec, or a wider
+	 * stream, left in it.
+	 */
+	memset(&ctx->codec.vp8, 0, sizeof(ctx->codec.vp8));
+
 	ctx->codec.vp8.entropy_probs_buf =
 		dma_alloc_coherent(dev->dev, CEDRUS_ENTROPY_PROBS_SIZE,
 				   &ctx->codec.vp8.entropy_probs_buf_dma,
